      <td>"Effective false positive rate" is user-centric — "any report a user did not want to see" — held
        under 5% against a 10% target. The predecessor FindBugs effort saw 84% of filed bugs go unfixed.</td>
      <td><strong>Real, but runs opposite to a naive reading.</strong> Tricorder's fix was to put the burden of
        making a finding <em>actionable</em> on the tool/process side, not to push more unverified claims onto
